# Secrets — never commit.
#
# A glob, not an enumeration. Listing `.env` and `.env.local` left
# `.env.production` and `.env.prod` trackable, confirmed with `git check-ignore`:
# an enumeration only covers the suffixes someone thought of. The negation is
# what keeps the one file that must stay committed.
.env*
!.env.example

# Cloudflare Wrangler (trigger/). `.dev.vars` is where wrangler puts secrets for
# local runs, so it would hold the GitHub PAT in plaintext; `.wrangler/` is local
# state. Listed before trigger/ was created rather than after — this repo has
# already published files it should not have, once. Globbed for the same reason
# as .env above: wrangler supports `.dev.vars.<environment>`, so
# `.dev.vars.production` was not covered.
.dev.vars*
.wrangler/
node_modules/

# Real people's names + contact channels (Gate 0.3).
# Health-adjacent product: do not publish these in a public repo.
# The committed structure lives in docs/distribution.example.md
docs/distribution.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Probe output / scratch
*.tmp
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# graphify knowledge-graph output. Generated, and graph.json embeds file
# content — regenerate with /graphify rather than committing it.
graphify-out/

# graphify's own exclude list. Scaffolding, and it names the private files by
# path, so it stays local for the same reason .claude/ does.
.graphifyignore

# AI-agent working files. Never publish these. The repo is a public portfolio
# piece and what belongs in it is the system — pipeline, schema, gates — not the
# scaffolding used to build it or private notes about the person building it.
#
#   .claude/     agent instructions, and the build plan, which carries personal
#                career context (placement timing, other projects, risk notes)
#   CLAUDE.md    agent operating instructions for this repo
#   IDEAS.md     the scope-creep parking lot — unbuilt ideas, not deliverables
#   PROGRESS.md  the build journal, written as interview preparation. It names
#                every mistake made here in the first person, for recall rather
#                than for publication; the README is the public account of the
#                same work.
#   PHASE2_PLAN.md  the agreed Phase 2 design, written to be handed to a fresh
#                agent session. Scaffolding for building, not a deliverable.
#                Root rather than docs/, because docs/ is otherwise entirely
#                published and one ignored file inside it is a trap for a
#                future push. Delete it once Gate 2 passes.
#
# They stay on disk and remain the authority for how the project is built. They
# are just not part of what is published.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
IDEAS.md
PROGRESS.md
PHASE2_PLAN.md

# Session handoffs written by the `handoff` skill. Same family as the files
# above: scaffolding for building, not a deliverable, and they quote the
# private ones. The whole directory, because there is one file per session.
Handoff/

# Local cache of pm25_history for scripts/baselines.py. Generated, ~10 MB, and
# rebuildable at any time with --refresh; the database is the source of truth.
# It exists because Neon bills per wake, so iterating on the baseline arithmetic
# against the database would be dozens of wakes for an answer that never changes.
data/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Fitted models and their model cards. Generated by scripts/benchmark.py and
# rebuildable from the gitignored history cache with a fixed seed. A fitted
# model is a build artefact, not source, and the card embeds a full pip freeze.
models/

# ML.pdf and anything else the to_pdf skill renders. Study and interview
# material, the same family as PROGRESS.md — the README is the public account of
# the same work.
TO-PDF/
